Subject: [PATCH 0/9] sparc32: repair HyperSPARC cache and kmap coherency

I am submitting nine HyperSPARC coherency fixes after the generic SPARC32
series. They cover instruction publication, cache-probe TLB cleanup,
index-based data maintenance, supervisor lines and kmap alias lifetimes.

I completed a native GDB 18.1 build on a dual-CPU HyperSPARC RT626
SPARCstation 20 with 512 MB RAM and a native SPARC32 SMP kernel containing
the combined fixes and optimizations, plus separate platform prerequisites.
I observed no core dumps, livelock or new kernel messages during the run.
This validates the combined integration, not each patch in isolation.
Individual patches retain their targeted test details.

Magnus Lindholm (9):
  sparc32: synchronize HyperSPARC instruction updates
  sparc32: discard HyperSPARC cache-probe TLB entries
  sparc32: flush HyperSPARC data ranges by index
  sparc32: flush HyperSPARC data pages by index
  sparc32: flush HyperSPARC pages to RAM by index
  sparc32: flush supervisor lines in the HyperSPARC whole-mm sweep
  sparc32: do not gate HyperSPARC cache cross-calls on mm_cpumask
  sparc32: flush all HyperSPARC colours for mapped folios
  sparc32: reconcile HyperSPARC local and persistent kmap aliases

